    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d644">

                <pb facs="1051" n="1037" xml:id="pg1037"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">756C.00/7–1950: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in France
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d644-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-22T17:00:00-04:00">July 22, 1950—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>413. Dept appreciates info contained Embtels
                    227, July 13 and 338, July 19.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d644-f2"/> However, Dept
                    believes that Emb’s statements contained in second from final para (ur 338),
                    particularly last sentence thereof, do not accurately reflect position this
                        Govt.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d644-f3"/> US recognizes sovereignty RUSI over all former Neth East Indies (save
                    regency Neth New Guinea) including territory of so-called “Rep of South
                    Moluccas”. We wld not countenance at this time participation by Amers in any
                    attempt to support or assist “Rep of South Moluccas” against the will or in
                    violation of laws of RUSI.</p>
                <p>You shld urgently communicate this view to rep mentioned Embtel 338.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d644-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>While Dept interested in Emb continued reporting this matter, Dept assumes Emb
                    aware fact that Nikijuluw undoubtedly using his contacts with Emb to his own
                    ends and presumably to those “Republic of South Moluccas” and that Emb is
                    exercising all due precautions in contacts it may have with him or others who
                    may be involved this question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d644-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d644-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Djakarta as 83 and to London as 417.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d644-f2" n="2" xml:id="d644-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed; they reported two approaches to Embassy Paris by J. P.
                    Nikijuluw, representative of the “Republic of South Moluccas.” (756C.00/7–1250
                    and 1950)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d644-f3" n="3" xml:id="d644-f3-content">
                <p>This sentence read: “The question of any American participation of such a scheme
                    [American citizens or capital in Ambon] would be judged on its merits if and
                    when it materialized.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d644-f4" n="4" xml:id="d644-f4-content">
                <p>In telegram 461, July 25, from Paris, not printed, the Department of State was
                    informed that the representative of the “Republic of South Moluccas” had been
                    told the views of the United States. (756C.00/7–2550)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
